#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Git v2.52 Release Notes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "UI, Workflows & Features"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:9
msgid ""
"The \"list\" subcommand of \"git refs\" acts as a front-end for \"git "
"for-each-ref\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:11
msgid "\"git cmd --help-all\" now works outside repositories."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:13
msgid "\"git diff-tree\" learned \"--max-depth\" option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:16
msgid ""
"A new subcommand \"git repo\" gives users a way to grab various repository "
"characteristics."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:19
msgid ""
"A new command \"git last-modified\" has been added to show the closest "
"ancestor commit that touched each path."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:22
msgid ""
"\"git refs exists\" that works like \"git show-ref --exists\" has been "
"added."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:26
msgid ""
"\"repo info\" learns a short-hand option \"-z\" that is the same as "
"\"--format=nul\", and learns to report the objects format used in the "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:30
msgid ""
"\"core.commentChar=auto\" that attempts to dynamically pick a suitable "
"comment character is non-workable, as it is too much trouble to support for "
"little benefit, and is marked as deprecated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:33
msgid ""
"\"git send-email\" learned to drive \"git imap-send\" to store already sent "
"e-mails in an IMAP folder."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:37
msgid ""
"The \"promisor-remote\" capability mechanism has been updated to allow the "
"\"partialCloneFilter\" settings and the \"token\" value to be communicated "
"from the server side."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:40
msgid ""
"Declare that \"git init\" that is not otherwise configured uses 'main' as "
"the initial branch, not 'master', starting Git 3.0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:43
msgid ""
"Keep giving hint about the default initial branch name for users who may be "
"surprised after Git 3.0 switch-over."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:46
msgid ""
"The stash.index configuration variable can be set to make \"git stash "
"pop/apply\" pretend that it was invoked with \"--index\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:49
msgid ""
"\"git fast-import\" learned that \"--signed-commits=<how>\" option that "
"corresponds to that of \"git fast-export\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:53
msgid ""
"Marking a hunk 'selected' in \"git add -p\" and then splitting made all the "
"split pieces 'selected'; this has been changed to make them all 'undecided', "
"which gives better end-user experience."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:57
msgid ""
"Configuration variables that take a pathname as a value "
"(e.g. blame.ignorerevsfile) can be marked as optional by prefixing "
"\":(optoinal)\" before its value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:59
msgid "Show 'P'ipe command in \"git add -p\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:63
msgid ""
"\"git sparse-checkout\" subcommand learned a new \"clean\" action to prune "
"otherwise unused working-tree files that are outside the areas of interest."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:66
msgid ""
"\"git fast-import\" is taught to handle signed tags, just like it recently "
"learned to handle signed commits, in different ways."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:69
msgid ""
"A new configuration variable commitGraph.changedPaths allows to turn "
"\"--changed-paths\" on by default for \"git commit-graph\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:72
msgid ""
"\"Symlink symref\" has been added to the list of things that will disappear "
"at Git 3.0 boundary."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:76
msgid ""
"\"git maintenance\" command learns the \"geometric\" strategy where it "
"avoids doing maintenance tasks that rebuilds everything from scratch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:78
msgid "\"git repo structure\", a new command."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:81
msgid ""
"The help text and manual page of \"git bisect\" command have been made "
"consistent with each other."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:84
#, no-wrap
msgid "Performance, Internal Implementation, Development Support etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:88
msgid ""
"string_list_split*() family of functions have been extended to simplify "
"common use cases."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:93
msgid ""
"Arrays of strbuf is often a wrong data structure to use, and strbuf_split*() "
"family of functions that create them often have better alternatives.  Update "
"several code paths and replace strbuf_split*()."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:98
msgid ""
"Revision traversal limited with pathspec, like \"git log dir/*\", used to "
"ignore changed-paths Bloom filter when the pathspec contained wildcards; now "
"they take advantage of the filter when they can."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:101
msgid ""
"Doc lint updates to encourage the newer and easier-to-use `synopsis` format, "
"with fixes to a handful of existing uses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:104
msgid ""
"Remove dependency on the_repository and other globals from the commit-graph "
"code, and other changes unrelated to de-globaling."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:107
msgid ""
"Discord has been added to the first contribution documentation as another "
"way to ask for help."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:111
msgid ""
"Inspired by Ezekiel's recent effort to showcase Rust interface, the hash "
"function implementation used to hash lines have been updated to the one used "
"for ELF symbol lookup by Glibc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:116
msgid ""
"Instead of scanning for the remaining items to see if there are still "
"commits to be explored in the queue, use khash to remember which items are "
"still on the queue (an unacceptable alternative is to reserve one object "
"flag bits)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:120
msgid ""
"The bulk-checkin code used to depend on a file-scope static singleton "
"variable, which has been updated to pass an instance throughout the "
"callchain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:124
msgid ""
"The work to build on the bulk-checkin infrastructure to create many objects "
"at once in a transaction and to abstract it into the generic object layer "
"continues."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:126
msgid "CodingGuidelines now spells out how bitfields are to be written."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:129
msgid ""
"Adjust to the way newer versions of cURL selectively enable tracing options, "
"so that our tests can continue to work."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:133
msgid ""
"The clear_alloc_state() API function was not fully clearing the structure "
"for reuse, but since nobody reuses it, replace it with a variant that frees "
"the structure as well, making the callers simpler."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:136
msgid ""
"\"git range-diff\" learned a way to limit the memory consumed by O(N*N) cost "
"matrix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:142
msgid ""
"Some places in the code confused a variable that is *not* a boolean to "
"enable color but is an enum that records what the user requested to do about "
"color.  A couple of bugs of this sort have been fixed, while the code has "
"been cleaned up to prevent similar bugs in the future."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:146
msgid ""
"The build procedure based on meson learned a target to only build "
"documentation, similar to \"make doc\".  (merge ff4ec8ded0 "
"ps/meson-build-docs later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:149
msgid ""
"Dip our toes a bit to (optionally) use Rust implemented helper called from "
"our C code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:152
msgid ""
"Documentation for \"git log --pretty\" options has been updated to make it "
"easier to translate."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:156
msgid ""
"Instead of three library archives (one for git, one for reftable, and one "
"for xdiff), roll everything into a single libgit.a archive.  This would help "
"later effort to FFI into Rust."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:158
msgid "The beginning of SHA1-SHA256 interoperability work."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:161
msgid ""
"Build procedure for a few credential helpers (in contrib/) have been "
"updated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:163
msgid "CI improvements to handle the recent Rust integration better."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:166
msgid ""
"The code in \"git repack\" machinery has been cleaned up to prepare for "
"incremental update of midx files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:169
msgid ""
"Two slightly different ways to get at \"all the packfiles\" in API has been "
"cleaned up."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:172
msgid "The code to walk revision graph to compute merge base has been optimized."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:174
msgid "AI guidelines has been added to our documentation set."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:177
msgid ""
"Contributed credential helpers (obviously in contrib/) now have \"cd $there "
"&& make install\" target."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:181
msgid ""
"The \"MyFirstContribution\" tutorial tells the reader how to send out their "
"patches; the section gained a hint to verify the message reached the mailing "
"list."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:184
msgid ""
"The \"debug\" ref-backend was missing a method implementation, which has "
"been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:187
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fixes since v2.51"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:191
msgid ""
"Unless otherwise noted, all the changes in 2.51.X maintenance track, "
"including security updates, are included in this release."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:194
msgid ""
"During interactive rebase, using 'drop' on a merge commit lead to an error, "
"which was incorrect."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:197
msgid ""
"\"git refs migrate\" to migrate the reflog entries from a refs backend to "
"another had a handful of bugs squashed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:202
msgid ""
"\"git remote rename origin upstream\" failed to move origin/HEAD to "
"upstream/HEAD when origin/HEAD is unborn and performed other renames "
"extremely inefficiently, which has been corrected.  (merge 16c4fa26b9 "
"ps/remote-rename-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:205
msgid ""
"\"git describe\" has been optimized by using better data structure.  (merge "
"08bb69d70f rs/describe-with-prio-queue later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:209
msgid ""
"\"git push\" had a code path that led to BUG() but it should have been a "
"die(), as it is a response to a usual but invalid end-user action to attempt "
"pushing an object that does not exist."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:212
msgid ""
"Various bugs about rename handling in \"ort\" merge strategy have been "
"fixed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:216
msgid ""
"\"git jump\" (in contrib/) fails to parse the diff header correctly when a "
"file has a space in its name, which has been corrected.  (merge 621ce9c1c6 "
"gh/git-jump-pathname-with-sp later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:222
msgid ""
"\"git diff --no-index\" run inside a subdirectory under control of a Git "
"repository operated at the top of the working tree and stripped the prefix "
"from the output, and oddballs like \"-\" (stdin) did not work correctly "
"because of it.  Correct the set-up by undoing what the set-up sequence did "
"to cwd and prefix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:228
msgid ""
"Various options to \"git diff\" that makes comparison ignore certain aspects "
"of the differences (like \"space changes are ignored\", \"differences in "
"lines that match these regular expressions are ignored\") did not work well "
"with \"--name-only\" and friends.  (merge b55e6d36eb "
"ly/diff-name-only-with-diff-from-content later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:230
msgid "The above caused regressions, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:233
msgid ""
"Documentation for \"git rebase\" has been updated.  (merge 3f7f2b0359 "
"je/doc-rebase later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:237
msgid ""
"The start_delayed_progress() function in the progress eye-candy API did not "
"clear its internal state, making an initial delay value larger than 1 second "
"ineffective, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:242
msgid ""
"The compatObjectFormat extension is used to hide an incomplete feature that "
"is not yet usable for any purpose other than developing the feature "
"further.  Document it as such to discourage its use by mere mortals."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:246
msgid ""
"\"git log -L...\" compared trees of multiple parents with the tree of the "
"merge result in an unnecessarily inefficient way.  (merge 0a15bb634c "
"sg/line-log-merge-optim later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:251
msgid ""
"Under a race against another process that is repacking the repository, "
"especially a partially cloned one, \"git fetch\" may mistakenly think some "
"objects we do have are missing, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:255
msgid ""
"\"git fetch\" can clobber a symref that is dangling when the remote-tracking "
"HEAD is set to auto update, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:259
msgid ""
"\"git describe <blob>\" misbehaves and/or crashes in some corner cases, "
"which has been taught to exit with failure gracefully.  (merge 7c10e48e81 "
"jk/describe-blob later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:262
msgid "Manual page for \"gitk\" is updated with the current maintainer's name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:266
msgid ""
"Update the instructions for using GGG in the MyFirstContribution document to "
"say that a GitHub PR could be made against `git/git` instead of "
"`gitgitgadget/git`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:269
msgid ""
"Makefile tried to run multiple \"cargo build\" which would not work very "
"well; serialize their execution to work around this problem."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:272
msgid ""
"\"git repack --path-walk\" lost objects in some corner cases, which has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:278
msgid ""
"\"git ls-files <pathspec>...\" should not necessarily have to expand the "
"index fully if a sparsified directory is excluded by the pathspec; the code "
"is taught to expand the index on demand to avoid this.  (merge 681f26bccc "
"ds/ls-files-lazy-unsparse later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:282
msgid ""
"Windows \"real-time monitoring\" interferes with the execution of tests and "
"affects negatively in both correctness and performance, which has been "
"disabled in Gitlab CI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:286
msgid ""
"A broken or malicious \"git fetch\" can say that it has the same object for "
"many many times, and the upload-pack serving it can exhaust memory storing "
"them redundantly, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:288
msgid "A corner case bug in \"git log -L...\" has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:293
msgid ""
"\"git rev-parse --short\" and friends failed to disambiguate two objects "
"with object names that share common prefix longer than 32 characters, which "
"has been fixed.  (merge 8655908b9e jc/longer-disambiguation-fix later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:297
msgid ""
"Some among \"git add -p\" and friends ignored color.diff and/or color.ui "
"configuration variables, which is an old regression, which has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:300
msgid ""
"\"git subtree\" (in contrib/) did not work correctly when splitting squashed "
"subtrees, which has been improved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:303
msgid ""
"Import a newer version of the clar unit testing framework.  (merge "
"93dbb6b3c5 ps/clar-updates later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:308
msgid ""
"\"git send-email --compose --reply-to=<address>\" used to add duplicated "
"Reply-To: header, which made mailservers unhappy.  This has been corrected.  "
"(merge f448f65719 nb/send-email-no-dup-reply-to later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:312
msgid ""
"\"git rebase -i\" failed to clean-up the commit log message when the command "
"commits the final one in a chain of \"fixup\" commands, which has been "
"corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:318
msgid ""
"There are double frees and leaks around setup_revisions() API used in \"git "
"stash show\", which has been fixed, and setup_revisions()  API gained a "
"wrapper to make it more ergonomic when using it with strvec-manged argc/argv "
"pairs.  (merge a04bc71725 jk/setup-revisions-freefix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:322
msgid ""
"Deal more gracefully with directory / file conflicts when the files backend "
"is used for ref storage, by failing only the ones that are involved in the "
"conflict while allowing others."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:325
msgid ""
"\"git last-modified\" operating in non-recursive mode used to trigger a "
"BUG(), which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:330
msgid ""
"The use of \"git config get\" command to learn how ANSI color sequence is "
"for a particular type, e.g., \"git config get --type=color --default=reset "
"no.such.thing\", isn't very ergonomic.  (merge e4dabf4fd6 "
"ps/config-get-color-fixes later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:334
msgid ""
"The \"do you still use it?\" message given by a command that is deeply "
"deprecated and allow us to suggest alternatives has been updated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:338
msgid ""
"Clang-format update to let our control macros be formatted the way we had "
"them traditionally, e.g., \"for_each_string_list_item()\" without space "
"before the parentheses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:341
msgid ""
"A few places where a size_t value was cast to curl_off_t without checking "
"has been updated to use the existing helper function."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:344
msgid ""
"\"git reflog write\" did not honor the configured user.name/email which has "
"been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:347
msgid ""
"Handling of an empty subdirectory of .git/refs/ in the ref-files backend has "
"been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:352
msgid ""
"Our CI script requires \"sudo\" that can be told to preserve environment, "
"but Ubuntu replaced with \"sudo\" with an implementation that lacks the "
"feature.  Work this around by reinstalling the original version."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:356
msgid ""
"The reftable backend learned to sanity check its on-disk data more "
"carefully.  (merge 466a3a1afd kn/reftable-consistency-checks later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:360
msgid ""
"A lot of code clean-up of xdiff.  Split out of a larger topic.  (merge "
"8b9c5d2e3a en/xdiff-cleanup later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:366
msgid ""
"\"git format-patch --range-diff=... --notes=...\" did not drive the "
"underlying range-diff with correct --notes parameter, ending up comparing "
"with different set of notes from its main patch output you would get from "
"\"git format-patch --notes=...\" for a singleton patch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:369
msgid ""
"The code in \"git add -p\" and friends to iterate over hunks was riddled "
"with bugs, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:373
msgid ""
"A few more things that patch authors can do to help maintainer to keep track "
"of their topics better.  (merge 1a41698841 tb/doc-submitting-patches later "
"to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:378
msgid ""
"An earlier addition to \"git diff --no-index A B\" to limit the output with "
"pathspec after the two directories misbehaved when these directories were "
"given with a trailing slash, which has been corrected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:383
msgid ""
"The \"--short\" option of \"git status\" that meant output for humans and "
"\"-z\" option to show NUL delimited output format did not mix well, and "
"colored some but not all things.  The command has been updated to color all "
"elements consistently in such a case."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:385
msgid "Unicode width table update."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:389
msgid ""
"GPG signing test set-up has been broken for a year, which has been "
"corrected.  (merge 516bf45749 jc/t1016-setup-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:394
msgid ""
"Recent OpenSSH creates the Unix domain socket to communicate with ssh-agent "
"under $HOME instead of /tmp, which causes our test to fail doe to overly "
"long pathname in our test environment, which has been worked around by using "
"\"ssh-agent -T\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:399
msgid ""
"strbuf_split*() to split a string into multiple strbufs is often a wrong API "
"to use.  A few uses of it have been removed by simplifying the code.  (merge "
"2ab72a16d9 ob/gpg-interface-cleanup later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:404
msgid ""
"\"git shortlog\" knows \"--committer\" and \"--author\" options, which the "
"command line completion (in contrib/) did not handle well, which has been "
"corrected.  (merge c568fa8e1c kf/log-shortlog-completion-fix later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:408
msgid ""
"\"git bisect\" command did not react correctly to \"git bisect help\" and "
"\"git bisect unknown\", which has been corrected.  (merge 2bb3a012f3 "
"rz/bisect-help-unknown later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:412
msgid ""
"The 'q'(uit) command in \"git add -p\" has been improved to quit without "
"doing any meaningless work before leaving, and giving EOF (typically "
"control-D) to the prompt is made to behave the same way."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:416
msgid ""
"The wildmatch code had a corner case bug that mistakenly makes \"foo**/bar\" "
"match with \"foobar\", which has been corrected.  (merge 1940a02dc1 "
"jk/match-pathname-fix later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:421
msgid ""
"Tests did not set up GNUPGHOME correctly, which is fixed but some flaky "
"tests are exposed in t1016, which needs to be addressed before this topic "
"can move forward.  (merge 6cd8369ef3 tz/test-prepare-gnupghome later to "
"maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:425
msgid ""
"The patterns used in the .gitignore files use backslash in the way "
"documented for fnmatch(3); document as such to reduce confusion.  (merge "
"8a6d158a1d jk/doc-backslash-in-exclude later to maint)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/RelNotes/2.52.0.adoc:429
msgid ""
"The version of macos image used in GitHub CI has been updated to macos-14, "
"as the macos-13 that we have been using got deprecated.  (merge 73b9cdb7c4 "
"jc/ci-use-macos-14 later to maint)."
msgstr ""

